Hi,

I want to estimate franciscana (Pontoporia blainvillei) bycatch for six different areas. The model was structured as follow:

formulaM3=y~0+Intercept+area+offset(LogRede)+f(s,model=spde)+f(Year,model="iid")

M3=inla(formulaM3,family="Poisson",data=inla.stack.data(stk.est),control.compute=list(dic=TRUE), control.predictor=(list(A=inla.stack.A(stk.est))))

My question is: How I do the prediction of franciscana bycatch for each area?

sim <- franciscanafit$sims.matrix

yarea1<- 1/(1+exp(-sim[,1]))

yarea2 <- 1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,2])))

yArea3 <- 1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,3])))

yArea4 <- 1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,4])))

yArea5 <- 1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,5])))

yArea6 <- 1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,6])))

The above code is just to give some idea that what I want to do. In the above code I have only one covariate (area) using R2winbugs package.

After the prediction of franciscana bycatch for each area, the total bycatch would be obtained multiplying by the total fishery effort.

