Hi,

My name is Jonatas and I would like to build a model to: 1) identify areas of higher risk of franciscana bycatch, and 2) estimate franciscana bycatch in the gillnet fishery. The model in INLA is structured as fallow:

  yi ~Poisson (λ)         where y is the number of franciscana incidentally captured in i gillnet sets (n= 1598).

formulaM<-y ~ 0 + Intercept+offset(Log_net_length)+

  f(s, model=spde)+f(Year,model="iid")+AREA2+AREA3+AREA4+AREA5+AREA6

M<-inla(formulaM,family="poisson",data=inla.stack.data(stk.est),control.compute=list(dic=TRUE), control.predictor=(list(A=inla.stack.A(stk.est))))

The first objective (prediction map of higher risk of bycatch) was already concluded. My doubt is related with bycatch estimation. I would like to know how I obtain the posterior distribution of franciscana bycatch for each area (1:6)?

Thanks,

Jonatas

